#: ../../adr/0018-web-interface.md:1
msgid "ADR-0018: Web interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0018-web-interface.md:3
msgid "**Status**: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0018-web-interface.md:4
msgid "**Date**: 2026-10-17"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0018-web-interface.md:5
msgid "**Plan step**: P14.1, P14.4 (REQ-WEB-1 to REQ-WEB-13, REQ-SVC-1)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0018-web-interface.md:7
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0018-web-interface.md:9
msgid ""
"The web interface lets people build a context with blocks, run it and "
"inspect its outputs without writing Python (UC5: a student opens the "
"public instance, loads a preset and follows a tutorial). It must give the"
" same results as the Python API and the AI assistant (objective O4), "
"serve a single user on their own machine as well as anonymous visitors on"
" a public server, and never let a web page drive real equipment without "
"authentication."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0018-web-interface.md:14
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0018-web-interface.md:16
msgid ""
"**Backend** `lumos.web`: a FastAPI application built by "
"`create_app(WebConfig)`, served by `lumos web` (uvicorn). Each route "
"translates one HTTP request into one call of `lumos.service.Service` "
"(ADR-0015) and nothing else; a `ServiceError` keeps its message, hint and"
" code and gets an HTTP status (`invalid` 400, `forbidden` 403, "
"`not_found` 404, `failed` 422, `quota` 429). The routes are under `/api` "
"(OpenAPI page at `/api/docs`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0018-web-interface.md:21
msgid ""
"**Sessions**: each browser gets an opaque random token in an `HttpOnly`, "
"`SameSite=Strict` cookie (`Secure` over HTTPS), bound to its own session "
"of the service (origin `web`). The token is not the identifier of the "
"service session. Sessions expire after an idle time and close their "
"contexts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0018-web-interface.md:24
msgid ""
"**Live updates**: the WebSocket `/api/ws` pushes the changes of the runs "
"of the session (status, progress) and the new entries of the journals of "
"its contexts (actions, runs, captured logs). It polls the service every "
"0.2 s: runs last seconds to minutes, and polling keeps the service free "
"of callbacks into an event loop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0018-web-interface.md:27
msgid ""
"**Local safety**: `lumos web` listens on `127.0.0.1` by default. In the "
"`local` profile the backend refuses HTTP requests addressed to a host "
"name other than `localhost`, `127.0.0.1` or `::1` (a page of another site"
" rebound to `127.0.0.1` by DNS cannot use it) and WebSockets opened from "
"a non-local origin (cookies are not enough to protect a WebSocket)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0018-web-interface.md:31
msgid ""
"**Palette**: `/api/palette` gives every element type with its JSON "
"Schema, its category (the second part of its identifier, "
"`lumos.<category>.<Name>`) and the hierarchy of the signal classes; the "
"frontend builds the palette, the forms and the typed connections from it,"
" with no code per element (REQ-WEB-2)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0018-web-interface.md:34
msgid ""
"**Frontend**: sources in `web/` (Vite, React, TypeScript, "
"`@xyflow/react`, Tailwind CSS, i18next, driver.js), built into "
"`src/lumos/web/static/` (not versioned) and served by the backend at `/`;"
" wheels and the Docker image are built with it. Without a build, `/` "
"explains how to build it and the API keeps working."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0018-web-interface.md:38
msgid "Alternatives considered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0018-web-interface.md:40
msgid ""
"Server-rendered pages (Jinja, HTMX): a graph editor needs a rich client; "
"React Flow is mature (§8.3)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0018-web-interface.md:41
msgid ""
"Server-sent events for progress: the WebSocket also serves the requests "
"of the client in later steps and is what REQ-WEB-5 names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0018-web-interface.md:43
msgid ""
"Storing the frontend build in git: generated files in reviews; the build "
"is reproducible with `npm ci`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0018-web-interface.md:44
msgid ""
"Calling the Python API from the routes: no parity by construction and "
"duplicated safeguards (ADR-0015)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0018-web-interface.md:46
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0018-web-interface.md:48
msgid ""
"Every feature added to the service is one route away from the web; the "
"web adds no physics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0018-web-interface.md:49
msgid ""
"Building a wheel or an image needs Node.js; `pip install -e .` from a "
"checkout works without it (API only)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0018-web-interface.md:50
msgid ""
"The authentication, roles and profiles of a public instance come next "
"(P14.2, P14.3, ADR-0019)."
msgstr ""

